# Regression script for the anatomy gate (see AnatomyCapability, Verb.RequiredCapabilities).
# Run: dotnet run -- --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters \
#        --period noon --observe-only flower --cli-timeout 500 \
#        --cli-script cli/beast_verbs.cli 2>&1 | grep '^\[cli\]'
# A non-zero exit means an `expect`/`wait` failed.
#
# The same object, looked at by two bodies. --observe-only pins the phase to the flower patch, and
# --fill-party gives the party a beast (the cat Nighthunter at seed 42) that the Speak About hand-off
# can pass narration to — the only way to make a companion the ACTING member, which is what the gate
# reads.
#
# GATHER is a Handcraft verb. The protagonist is offered it on the patch; the cat, with the same
# patch in front of it, is not — the goal is not in its list at all, so `goal gather` falls back and
# stdout carries
#   [debug] --goal-only 'gather': no such goal here — drawing from all N.
# (An absence cannot be asserted on screen: `expect` scans the whole terminal, greyed history and all.)
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Field" --period noon --observe-only "Test Berry Bush"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]

# --- the human: gather is offered, and the action line says so ------------------
strategy succeed
goal gather
# Clicked by INDEX, not by name: under --playground the clickable keyword is the object's
# own noun, not its display name, so a phase pinned with --observe-only still cannot be
# spelled. Index means "whatever this phase opened on".
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect gather

# --- hand narration to the beast, on the same object ----------------------------
# Straight from the same live keyword — do NOT press the footer here: with the action offered but
# not taken, the phase is idle and that button reads LEAVE, which walks out of the location.
click keyword 0
choose 2
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect [NIGHTHUNTER]

# --- the beast: no gather in its goals, but it still acts ------------------------
# The spoken address leaves its own keyword live ('colour-clusters' at this seed) and it points at the
# same flower patch. `goal gather` prints the fallback line above; the phase then runs on whatever the
# cat CAN do, which proves the gate narrowed the goal list rather than emptying it.
goal gather
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect [NIGHTHUNTER]
state

# This script tests an ABSENCE: the cat must NOT be offered gather. `--goal-only gather` finding
# no such goal is therefore the assertion passing, so its miss must not fail the run.
allow-flag-miss --goal-only
quit
